        <briefdescription>
<para>What to do with a query outside of the interpolation domain. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The Boost cardinal B-splines are not consistent about this: the quadratic and quintic ones reject such a query, while the cubic one extrapolates. Each interpolator picks the behaviour of the cardinal implementation it shares its name with, so that which of the two paths is taken stays invisible to the caller. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
